  "name": "Sooauth",
  "abstract": "Open-source, lightweight OpenID Provider in a single Go binary, aimed at indie developers and teams building with AI coding assistants. Apps sign users in through hosted pages using the authorization code flow with PKCE and verify JWTs against a JWKS endpoint, so no auth tables live in the app database. It supports passwords, passkeys, Google and GitHub sign-in, TOTP with backup codes, refresh token rotation, signed webhooks, per-project theming and custom email providers. Each project is an isolated tenant. Available as a cloud service at auth.sooauth.com (free during public beta) or self-hosted with Docker, PostgreSQL and Redis under AGPL-3.0. SAML, SCIM and audit exports are only offered on the Enterprise plan.",
